Roasted Brussels sprouts, about 40 small pieces (many look halved or loose leaves). Each weighs roughly 8-10 g, so the total is about 300 g? That seems high for the plate. They are small, around 2-3 cm across, so about 7 g each. 40 × 7 ≈ 280 g, but I'll estimate about 200 g to allow for small sprouts.

Roasted with oil, they run about 70 kcal per 100 g, which gives roughly 140-150 kcal.

